To convert a `flutter::EncodableValue` to a `std::string` in Flutter, you can use the `flute::JSONValueEncoder` class to encode the `EncodableValue` as a JSON string. Here's an example of how to achieve this:

```cpp
#include <flutter/encodable_value.h>
#include <flutter/json_method_codec.h>

std::string encodeFlutterValueToString(const flutter::EncodableValue& value) {
  flutter::JSONValueEncoder encoder;
  std::vector<uint8_t> encoded;
  encoder.Encode(&value, &encoded);
  return std::string(encoded.begin(), encoded.end());
}
```

In the example above, the `encodeFlutterValueToString` function takes a `flutter::EncodableValue` as input and uses the `flutter::JSONValueEncoder` to encode it as a JSON string. The encoded data is then converted to a `std::string` and returned.

