Here is a C function that returns the number of distinct values in the given array:

```c
int solution(int* A, int N) {
  qsort(A, N, sizeof(int), compare);

  int distinct = 1;
  for(int i=1; i<N; i++) {
    if(A[i] != A[i-1]) 
      distinct++;
  }

  return distinct;
}

int compare(const void *a, const void *b) {
  return (*(int*)a - *(int*)b);
}
```

The algorithm:

1. Sort the array using qsort with a compare function to sort integers. This takes O(NlogN) time.

2. Iterate through the sorted array and count the number of times the current element is different from the previous. Each different element implies a distinct value. 

3. Return the distinct count.

This algorithm has O(NlogN) time complexity due to sorting and O(1) additional space complexity.

